    "created_at": "2023-04-14T17:01:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-14T17:01:00Z",
    "body": "> Does it make sense to fire all of the events in this case?\r\n\r\nWe discussed this at great length during the spec PR review. The problem is that events can't be fired synchronously during removal, so we'd have to queue the events in this case, which leads to myriad problems like out of order events. So we decided that the best course of action was not firing events in this case.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
